      'Malone\'s cost included the burden of building a major company in a system that offered Black women few protections. Her business success made her visible, but legal disputes, divorce, competition, and economic change placed pressure on what she built. She also carried the cost of later erasure, as public memory often collapsed Black beauty entrepreneurship into a single name.',
      'Her impact was structural. Poro trained workers, created income, expanded Black women\'s entrepreneurship, and helped turn beauty culture into a serious economic field. Her philanthropy also supported children and families beyond the marketplace.'
